BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hands-On Dinosaur Fossils & Ancient Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T110000
UID:6a98263f2dac6e00372377c8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an opportunity to handle\, examine up close and di
 scuss nine real and replica fossils in this fascinating hands-on workshop.
  Participants will be entertained and educated\, not just about the fossil
 s themselves\, but the paleontological aspects that underpin them. Concept
 s include: evolution\, fossilization\, ‘The Tree of Life’ (phylogeny) 
 and — of course — dinosaurs!
LOCATION:York Woods\, First Floor Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a98263f2dac6e00372377c8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Five Pieces of the AI Puzzle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T193000
UID:6a7d0bcabe1482002986fb97@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This interactive 60-minute session demystifies artificial inte
 lligence through a unique five-piece puzzle framework\, guiding participan
 ts to better understand AI’s presence\, challenge common perceptions\, 
 and actively shape how they live and work alongside it. Combining multimed
 ia\, collaboration\, and real-world examples\, the program empowers audien
 ces to move beyond passive awareness toward confident\, informed engagemen
 t with AI.\nThis is a multi-media presentation with video clips\, props\, 
 group discussion and begins with an opening Puzzle Pieces song and an act
 ual solve a 5-piece puzzle challenge ice breaker.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl
 .ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7d0bcabe1482002986fb97
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
