BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Become a Volunteer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T150000
UID:6a469808c52cdc3600ee5f3c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A general session\, intended for the volunteer seekers who are
  new to volunteering\, or in need to understand the process of formal vol
 unteering. This session caters for all demographics.\nThis session will b
 e presented by a representative from Volunteer Toronto.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a469808c52cdc3600ee5f3c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T180000
UID:69c30ab6b48451fc3c0b0936@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. It involves peer-led group activities including 
 crafts\, games\, walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\, build connect
 ions\, and tell us about programs and services you would like to see in th
 e neighbourhood!\nJoin Therapy Dog Pierre who visits Parliament alternate
  Mondays from 4:30-5:30 pm.\nRefreshments provided.\nThis program is in co
 llaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd Floor Last Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c30ab6b48451fc3c0b0936
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
