DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T150000
UID:6a8f68ca3b6c71003e5ba279@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nJoin us at the crafts & games ta
 ble\, or for a community walk (weather permitting).\nVisit with a therapy 
 dog!\nOzzy is here August 31\,\nSeptember 21\, October 5 + 19.\nSnacks 
 and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will 
 be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGers
 tein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f68ca3b6c71003e5ba279
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Life Skills: Using a Cell Phone
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261108T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261108T160000
UID:6a948abc69166f088b960aa2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Using a cellphone is a life skill! Learn about the basics of u
 sing a cell phone in a relaxed\, drop in setting. In this class we will co
 ver all of the different  parts of a basic smart phone\, the operating sys
 tem\, the home page and how to use Wi-Fi and Cellular Data. We will practi
 ce skills such as taking a picture\, scanning a QR code\, and sending a te
 xt.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a948abc69166f088b960aa2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
