BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Horror Classics on Film: Pulse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T130000
UID:6a98423a3b6c71003e5d2cdd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join author Allison Rumfitt and filmmaker David Prior as they 
 discuss Kiyoshi Kurosawa's techno-thriller masterpiece with host Adam Naym
 an.\nIn this first instalment of Toronto Public Library's virtual series o
 n Horror Classics on Film\, writer and critic Alison Rumfitt\, filmmaker D
 avid Prior\, and host Adam Nayman discuss Pulse\, Kiyoshi Kurosawa's sinis
 ter techno-thriller film.\nImagining a world where the internet becomes a 
 breeding ground for malevolent spirits\, the film's artistry lies in the s
 pine-tingling power of suggestion rather than a barrage of blood and guts.
  This conversation will explore the lasting relevance and lingering imager
 y behind the film.\nAbout this event's guests:\nAlison Rumfitt\nis a write
 r and cultural critic. Her two horror novels Tell Me I'm Worthless and Bra
 inwyrms push the boundaries of both taste and form to the shock of readers
  everywhere. She has written for Little White Lies and Dazed\, and intervi
 ewed new Doctor Ncuti Gatwa for Rolling Stone. She's considered herself a 
 fan of Doctor Who ever since her father played her the theme song to scare
  her when she was about five years old.\nDavid Prior\nis an American filmm
 aker\, best known for his work on the cult horror film The Empty Man\, and
  television series such as Voir and Guillermo del Toro's Cabinet of Curios
 ities. He has also directed and produced making-of documentaries for films
 \, most notably the works of David Fincher and Michael Bay.\nAdam Nayman\n
 is a critic\, teacher\, and author\, whose books include critical surveys 
 of the Coen Brothers\, Paul Thomas Anderson\, and most recently\, in Mind 
 Games\, the filmmaker David Fincher. He is a regular contributor to The Ri
 nger\, a lecturer at the University of Toronto's Cinema Studies Institute\
 , and he has written on film for The New Yorker and The New York Times.\nR
 ead more:\nTell Me I'm Worthless\nBrainwyrms\n***\nImportant information f
 or accessing this live virtual event:\nYou must register for a free ticket
  via Eventbrite to gain access to this event.\nThis event will be presente
 d in a Zoom Webinar. Once registered\, you will receive reminder emails fr
 om both Zoom and Eventbrite with links and instructions to access your uni
 que Zoom Webinar link to watch this event.\nAt the time of the event\, you
  must be signed in to Zoom or Eventbrite with the same email address that 
 you used to book your ticket in order to access your unique event link. Un
 ique event links can only be open on one device at a time.\n***\nAccessibi
 lity at Toronto Public Library\nWe are committed to making our content acc
 essible to as many Torontonians as possible. Please call or email us if yo
 u are Deaf or have a disability and would like to request accommodation to
  participate in this program. Please let us know as far in advance as poss
 ible and we will do our best to meet your request. At least three weeks' n
 otice is preferred. Phone 416-393-7099 or email accessibleservices@tpl.ca\
 n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.\nRegistrants
  may be contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program\n. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a98423a3b6c71003e5d2cdd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CRA Tax Information Session for Self-employed Small Business Owner
 s (T1)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T140000
UID:6a96f683aafa61002960b42e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This Canada Revenue Agency presentation is for unincorporated 
 small business owners and self-employed individuals looking for free tax h
 elp.\nA CRA Liaison Officer will cover:\n- Business tax deductions\n- Comm
 on tax errors\n- Helpful tools and services offered by the CRA\n- General 
 bookkeeping concepts and best practices\n***\nThis 2-hour program is held 
 online via CRA's MS Teams. Please register to receive information on how t
 o attend (an event reminder email will be sent approximately 24 hours 
 before the event begins).\nThis program will not be recorded. Captions wil
 l be available.\n***\nAdditional CRA Info Sessions\nWe also offer an addi
 tional CRA Tax Information Session for Self-employed Small Business Owners
  (T1) on\nTuesday\, October 13\, 2026 - 6:30 to 8:30 pm\n.\nLooking for a
  CRA info session for small corporations (T2)? We also offer them on:\nTue
 sday\, October 20\, 2026 - 6:30 to 8:30 pm\nThursday\, October 22\, 2026 -
  12:00 to 2:00 pm\nNeed help with MS Teams?\nJoining a Teams Meeting\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96f683aafa61002960b42e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T153000
UID:6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61de2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet weekly\,\nin-person\,\nevery Tuesday afternoon\, Se
 ptember 15 - December 8\, 2-3:30 PM (12 sessions).\nParticipants are expec
 ted to commit to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekl
 y basis.\nLearners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digita
 l badge\ndownload a certificate of completion
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61de2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T150000
UID:6a8f68ca3b6c71003e5ba273@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nJoin us at the crafts & games ta
 ble\, or for a community walk (weather permitting).\nVisit with a therapy 
 dog!\nOzzy is here August 31\,\nSeptember 21\, October 5 + 19.\nSnacks 
 and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will 
 be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGers
 tein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f68ca3b6c71003e5ba273
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
