DESCRIPTION:Come and join us on the second Wednesday of every month to dis
 cuss a variety of books.\nEveryone is welcome! Drop-in\, no registration r
 equired.\n2026 Reading List:\nJanuary 14:\nWhat I Mean to Say\n: Remaking 
 Conversation in Our Time by Ian Williams\nFebruary 11:\nFahrenheit 451\nby
  Ray Bradbury\nMarch 11:\nThe Remains of the Day\nby Kazuo Ishiguro\nApril
  8:\nOrbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nMay 13:\nThe Empusium\n: A Health Resort
  Horror Story by Olga Tokarczuk\nJune 10:\nTruth Telling\nSeven Conversati
 ons About Indigenous Life in Canada by Michelle Good\nJuly 8:\nThree Days 
 in June\nby Anne Tyler\nAugust 12:\nThe Woman in the Library\nby Sulari Ge
 ntill\nSeptember 9:\nValentine in Montreal\nby Heather O'Neill\nOctober 14
 :\nOn Tyranny: Twenty Lessons from the Twentieth Century\nby Timothy Snyde
 r\nNovember 11: Five Tuesdays in Winter by Lily King\nDecember 9: Best Bo
 oks of the Year Discussion
