BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hazel Mae: Before I Let You Go
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T200000
UID:6a85b6abf564ef0d72c0eb1f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Beloved Toronto Blue Jays sportscaster Hazel Mae shares her op
 en and insightful new memoir\, in conversation with Ernie Clement.\nIn Bef
 ore I Let You Go\, Mae invites us into a candid\, behind-the-scenes look a
 t her life\, from her early days in the Philippines to her arrival in Cana
 da and her rise through the ranks of sports journalism.\nWith warmth and w
 it\, she reflects on breaking into broadcasting\, navigating the US sports
  media scene\, returning home to cover the Toronto Blue Jays\, and masteri
 ng the art of the post game interview—often while dodging celebratory Ga
 torade showers.\nHazel Mae speaks with Toronto Blue Jay Ernie Clement abo
 ut her memoir and life as one of Canada's most recognizable broadcasters.\
 nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purchase.\nAbout this
  event’s guests:\nHazel Mae\nErnie Clement\nRead more:\nBefore I Let You
  Go : My Life in Broadcasting\, Baseball\, and Beyond\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISI
 T:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789
  Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm
 .\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell thes
 e events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportunity 
 to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. S
 eating first come\, first served.\nBar:\nBeer/wine available for purchase 
 (debit/credit only).\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Seri
 es\n\, where we host local and international authors\, artists and thinker
 s in conversation about their new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
