SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Mona Labib
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260902T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T235959
UID:6a8c4ef3be1482002989995a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of September\, works by artist Mona Labib
  are on display at Agincourt Branch.\nMona Labib is a professional IT Proj
 ect Manager who loves the arts. Most of her works are in oil. Throughout h
 er career\, arts and painting provided an escape from the daily stresses 
 of her job and a means of relaxation. Although she has been painting and t
 aking art lessons for many years\, she still considers herself very much 
 a beginner.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. T
 oronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their wo
 rk at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse
  cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can b
 e viewed during Agincourt branch open hours. Please check the\nAgincourt\
 nbranch page before your visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Mon
 a Labib\; oil\; "Where the Sun Meets the Tide"
LOCATION:Agincourt\, First floor hallway
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4ef3be1482002989995a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
