SUMMARY:Randy Boyagoda: Lords of Serendipity
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260911T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260911T200000
UID:6a85b730fa71a30d92946b60@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents novelist Randy Boyagoda in conversation with Paru
 l Sehgal at the Toronto Reference Library's Appel Salon.\nIn his wildly fu
 nny and richly observed new novel\nLords of Serendipity\n\, acclaimed auth
 or Randy Boyagoda delivers the twenty-first-century global campus novel\, 
 a story that spans contemporary Sri Lanka and the United States\, followin
 g two teenage girls with similar collegiate ambitions. What does the globa
 l scramble for elite education reveal about class\, ambition\, and inequal
 ity today? How do institutions meant to open doors so often become sites o
 f exploitation\, for domestic and international students\, for parents\, f
 or those gatekeepers and intermediaries trying to extract as much as they 
 offer?\nDrawing on his own decades inside the academy as an English profes
 sor and U of T's first-ever Advisor on Civil Discourse\, Boyagoda brings a
  novelist's eye and a scholar's insight to this wicked\, humane satire of 
 careerism\, hope\, and the lengths we'll go to for the people we love.\nJo
 in one of Canada's most celebrated literary novelists\, in conversation wi
 th acclaimed critic Parul Sehgal\, for an evening exploring ambition\, ine
 quality\, and the absurd theatre of higher education in the twenty-first c
 entury.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purchase.\nAb
 out this event’s guests:\nRandy Boyagoda\nParul Sehgal\nRead more:\nLord
 s of Serendipity : A Novel\nDante's Indiana\nOriginal Prin\n***\nPLAN YOUR
  VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library
  (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7
 :00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell
  these events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportu
 nity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reach
 ed. Seating first come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available for pur
 chase (debit/credit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibil
 ity. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to request accomm
 odation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-3
 93-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nThis event is part 
 of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local and international a
 uthors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about their new books and bi
 g ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Reg
 istrants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey following the program
 . Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed
  to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Stree
 t\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram and Bluma Appel Salon\, Toronto 
 Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b730fa71a30d92946b60
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
