BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Customer Segmentation: Who Will Actually Pay?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T200000
UID:6a99ba96b88596143287d991@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The fastest way to start a new business is to try to sell it t
 o everybody. This session will teach you to narrow down your target group 
 by using geography\, demographics\, and behavioral statistics to determine
  demand. It will also cover how to spot your early adopters\, i.e.\, the p
 eople who need what you're building most will be flexible while you get it
  right. We'll discover how to narrow down your target audience\, and how t
 o determine if you were well informed in your decisions.\nRegistration rec
 ommended. Drop-ins are welcomed until room capacity is reached.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99ba96b88596143287d991
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Business Idea Validation: Can I Make Money with This?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T200000
UID:6a99ba0b660e510bf441022f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:"Everyone I talked to said they loved it" is the most expensiv
 e sentence in business. This session teaches you how to test an idea prope
 rly by identifying fatal assumptions\, designing theoretical prototypes\, 
 and engaging customers in conversations that produce honest answers. We'll
  cover pre-sales\, waitlists\, and other ways to get evidence before you b
 uild anything. You'll practice the technique in front of other participant
 s and leave with a better idea of your next steps.\nRegistration required\
 , limited room capacity.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founders Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99ba0b660e510bf441022f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Entrepreneurship: Is This for Me\, and Where Do I 
 Start?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T200000
UID:6a99b901d94765189bb97c31@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Most people don't hesitate because their idea is bad. They hes
 itate because they think entrepreneurship is intimidating. This opening se
 ssion challenges this assumption by using real Canadian statistics and int
 roducing the Business Model Canvas\, both of which can help you capture ho
 w a business creates value\, reaches customers\, and generates capital. By
  the end of this session\, you will be given a chance to start filling in 
 your own Business Model Canvas and a chance to network with other particip
 ants.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins are welcomed until room capacity
  is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Novella\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
