BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: The Fragile Wild — Photographs by Roshan Pan
 jwani
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T235959
UID:6a875a463b6c71003e5a39be@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of September\, the works of photographer
  Roshan Panjwani are on display at\nDeer Park branch\n.\nRoshan Panjwani
  is a Toronto-based nature and wildlife photographer\, originally from Ind
 ia. Living with a physical disability has meant approaching fieldwork diff
 erently and has reinforced the persistence the work demands. Over more tha
 n a decade he has photographed across a wide range of habitats: the tiger 
 reserves of India\, the Okavango Delta and salt pans of Botswana\, the sav
 annahs of East Africa\, the Himalayan high desert of Ladakh\, the rainfore
 sts of Costa Rica\, the mountains and coast of Alaska and the Canadian Roc
 kies\, and the High Arctic fjords of Greenland and Svalbard. His photograp
 hs have appeared on the cover of Canadian Photography magazine\, been feat
 ured by BBC Earth\, and appear in Europe's Sea Mammals\, published by Prin
 ceton University Press. Through his work he hopes to deepen appreciation a
 nd care for the planet's fragile ecosystems and the wildlife inhabiting th
 em.\n"I photograph nature and wildlife in some of the world's less-explore
 d places — pristine habitats\, distinctive species\, and landscapes that
  can feel otherworldly. Much of my work entails long hours in the field\, 
 watching for the light to shift or for wildlife behaviour that makes the f
 rame memorable."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogra
 m. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit thei
 r work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the div
 erse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit c
 an be viewed during Deer Park's open hours. Please check the\nDeer Park br
 anch\npage before your visit. The branch will be closed on September 6th 
 and 7th.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit\nPhotographer: Roshan Panjw
 ani\nTitle of Piece: King of Ice\nMedium: Fine art pigment print\, face-m
 ounted to acrylic\nSize/Dimensions: 30" x 45"
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a875a463b6c71003e5a39be
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
