BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261002T160000
UID:6a75ee8da5e5f025a9cea649@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\, Friday September 11\, 18\, 25 and Oct 2\, from 1:30-4PM.
 \nRegistration is a two-step process. First\, participants must complete t
 heir registration through this page. After this step\, library staff will 
 follow up to request additional information in order to complete the regis
 tration.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a75ee8da5e5f025a9cea649
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T153000
UID:6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61dda@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet weekly\,\nin-person\,\nevery Tuesday afternoon\, Se
 ptember 15 - December 8\, 2-3:30 PM (12 sessions).\nParticipants are expec
 ted to commit to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekl
 y basis.\nLearners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digita
 l badge\ndownload a certificate of completion
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61dda
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library:  Cardinal Flower Felt Collage
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T200000
UID:6a7f610360ccaf01c01e449d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 3 of a series of workshops for adults\, exploring local f
 lora through embroidery and felt collage. Hosted by Artist in the Library\
 , Sarah Zanchetta.\nRegistration is required. Space is limited.\nPlease no
 te: Registered participant spaces will be held for 15 minutes after which 
 drop-ins will be allowed.\nMeet the Resident:\nSarah Zanchetta (she/they) 
 is a queer textile artist and educator whose practice dives into the loss 
 of connection and knowledge of poisonous plants in North America. Zanchett
 a uses textiles\, texts\, and hosts community workshops to create intimate
  works and spaces where we can unfold our curiosities\, care and anxieties
  about what grows beside our feet. She holds a Master of Visual Studies f
 rom the University of Toronto (2023) and a BFA from OCAD University (2018)
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7f610360ccaf01c01e449d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk with Dr. Kirsten Johnson on Humanitarienne: A Doctor
 ’s Stories from the Conflict Zone
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T110000
UID:6a9887195e6fc10d0550f26a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As a physician and public health specialist\,\nDr. Kirsten Joh
 nson\nhas led missions in conflict zones\, disaster-stricken regions and u
 nderserved communities. In her book\,\nHumanitarienne: A Doctor's Stories 
 from the Conflict Zone\n\, she traces how a strict childhood marked by tra
 uma pushed her to seek independence early.\nJoin this 1-hour presentation 
 where Johnson shares her story as a global health expert working in some o
 f the world's most volatile places and how she pushed back on inequities e
 mbedded in humanitarian systems. If you're drawn to international work\, s
 ocial justice\, or the ways in which people are shaped by—and in turn sh
 ape the world around them\, this presentation will inspire you.\nPresented
  as part of Women's History Month.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual event is f
 ree to join and will take place on\nZoom\n.\nRegister to receive an email
  with details on how to join the session and to get a link to the recordin
 g.\nCaptions will be available.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and part
 icipating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nPlace a hold or bo
 rrow from Toronto Public Library:\nHumanitarienne: A Doctor's Stories from
  the Conflict Zone - Link coming soon.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9887195e6fc10d0550f26a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
