BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laverne Cox: Transcendent
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T200000
UID:6a85b52d4c610f0038954edd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Four-time Emmy-nominated actress Laverne Cox shares her journe
 y from working as a struggling actress to leading a cultural movement.\nLa
 verne Cox is a powerhouse in the fight for transgender rights and represen
 tation—but her path from a struggling trans actress to a cultural moveme
 nt was anything but easy.\nIn Transcendent\, Laverne invites us into her j
 ourney as a transgender woman in Hollywood\; confronting childhood trauma\
 , shame and feelings of unworthiness\; and\, ultimately\, healing.\nLavern
 e Cox speaks with author and activist Kai Cheng Thom about making history 
 for her role in Orange is the New Black\, her fearless advocacy for LGBTQ+
  rights and finding her voice in a world that can too often feel lonely an
 d unaccepting.\nQ&A to follow. Books available for purchase.\nAbout this e
 vent’s guests:\nLaverne Cox\nKai Cheng Thom\nRead more:\nTranscendent\nF
 alling Back in Love With Being Human\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nCo
 ncourse Event Space\, North York Central Library (5120 Yonge St)\nTime:\nD
 oors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration requi
 red.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the greatest
  number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 
 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\n*
 **\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host lo
 cal and international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about
  their new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief surve
 y following the program. Questions about how the library handles your info
 rmation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b52d4c610f0038954edd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
