BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Python Essentials 1 and 2 Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T153000
UID:6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5ca@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn Python and build your programming skills in a supportive
  group. This learning circle will meet on Tuesday afternoons from Septemb
 er 22 to December 8\, 2-3:30pm. Learning circles are study groups guided b
 y staff for people who want to take a free online course together in a wel
 coming space. Learners meet weekly and work together through the course ma
 terials. Participants are expected to commit to the duration of the course
  and attend all learning circle sessions.\nLearners who successfully compl
 ete both courses will earn a digital badge and certificate of completion.\
 nPython Essentials 1\nis the first in a 2-course series that teaches compu
 ter programming skills including how to design\, develop\, and improve com
 puter programs using the Python programming language. The course covers es
 sential programming topics such as data types\, variables\, control flow\,
  functions\, and exceptions.\nPython Essentials 2\nis the second in a 2-co
 urse series that will prepare you for the PCAP – Certified Associate in 
 Python Programming certification exam at Pearson VUE. This intermediate-le
 vel course covers advanced aspects of Python programming\, including modul
 es\, packages\, exceptions\, file processing and object-oriented programmi
 ng (OOP).\nFor more information about the Python learning circle\, please 
 contact\nnetworkingacademy@tpl.ca\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:York Woods
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7cd1d22dac6e00371ea5ca
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: "Captain Toronto" works by Danilo Ursini
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T235959
UID:6a99adaab20478002997cafb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of September\, works by artist Danilo Urs
 ini are on display at Don Mills Branch in an exhibit titled Reflections o
 f Nature.\nDanilo Ursini is an Italian artist specializing in graphic nove
 ls\, with a focus on the Captain Toronto series. His work blends superhero
  storytelling with\nthe unique culture and identity of Toronto. He has sho
 wcased  art in major exhibitions\, gaining recognition for my distinctive
  approach to both narrative\nand visual design. Currently\, he continues t
 o explore and expand the Captain Toronto universe\, aiming to capture the 
 essence of the city and its people.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Ex
 hibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local art
 ists to exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits ai
 m to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourh
 oods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Don Mills branch open hours. Ple
 ase check the\nDon Mills\nbranch page before you visit.\nFree. All are wel
 come.
LOCATION:Don Mills
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99adaab20478002997cafb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Calm and Colour - featuring a therapy dog
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T160000
UID:6a47b839541102b7fa8a2b90@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a “We Are All Related” Indigenous themed comm
 unity colouring activity led by One Health Partners in partnership with T
 oronto Public Library. Participants will get an opportunity to color indi
 vidual prints designed by Indigenous artist Caitlin Wemigwans\, which will
  be placed on a "Tree of Belonging" celebrating the interconnectedness of 
 all life\n—\nan important part of Indigenous culture as well as One Heal
 th Partners philosophy.\nThe session also features a\ntherapy dog\nand\nha
 ndler team\nfrom One Health Partners\, providing comfort\, calm and joy.
  Participants will be invited to gently interact with the dog in small gr
 oups of up to 5 people at a time.\nRegistrants will need to check-in by 3:
 05 pm to hold their spot. Drop-ins welcome until capacity is reached.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a47b839541102b7fa8a2b90
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
