BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ready to Launch: Keeping the Momentum and Finding the Money
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6a99bba4341bb11431eea279@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:We're wrapping up our 2026 Entrepreneur in Residence program w
 ith a final session on launching your business. We'll map the real funding
  landscape for a new business in Ontario — startup loans\, microloans\, 
 grants\, sponsorship and revenue-based approaches — and cover what each 
 one requires\, so you don't waste months applying to the wrong thing. You'
 ll learn how to present your business to a funder\, and where to find free
  ongoing support once the series ends. We'll close with the accountability
  habits that keep a new business moving.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-i
 ns welcomed until room capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bba4341bb11431eea279
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tools to Run Your Business
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T200000
UID:6a99bb28660e510bf4410247@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For new business owners\, staying organized can be just as cha
 llenging to find customers. This session will explore the tools that can t
 ake routine work off your plate. From bookkeeping and invoicing\, to sched
 uling\, payments\, customer records\, marketing\, and social media creatio
 n. We will also look at where AI tools can genuinely help save time and ad
 d value versus making unnecessary work. We'll discover where to find free 
 resources\, and how to avoid subscribing to services that won't be of valu
 e in the long run. You'll leave with a concise list of tools appropriate f
 or new business owners.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins welcomed until
  room capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99bb28660e510bf4410247
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
