BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start & Grow Your Business with TSBEC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T193000
UID:69e26e4cdefec6489cbe72a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Information session on how to start\, plan\, finance\, and gro
 w your very own small business.\nOwning a business is a dream for many peo
 ple. Every new business starts with an idea. This interactive presentation
  will give an overview of how to make it happen and the opportunity to ask
  questions related to your business. An advisor from the Toronto Small Bus
 iness Enterprise Center (TSBEC) will present an overview of information r
 elated to the business planning process\, evaluating a business idea\, fin
 ancing\, marketing planning\, business structures\, regulatory requirement
 s\, and more.\nRegistration is encouraged. Drop-ins welcome until capacity
  is reached.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st Fl
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e26e4cdefec6489cbe72a7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Managing Invasive Plants Around Your Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T183000
UID:6a6231364523092f00320c63@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for a presentation o
 n invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. Learn how to ide
 ntify these species\, understand their impact\, and how to manage them.\nY
 ou’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing n
 ative habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeowners\, and anyone interested
  in urban ecology.\nNo registration required. This is a drop-in program.\n
 This program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, suppor
 ted by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6231364523092f00320c63
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
