BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marina Nemat: Mistress of the Persian Boarding House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T200000
UID:6a85b7952cbfe80d71a47342@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents internationally bestselling author Marina Nemat i
 n conversation with Farah Heron at the North York Central Library's Concou
 rse Event Space.\nIn her debut work of historical fiction\, Mistress of th
 e Persian Boarding House\, Nemat turns to the extraordinary life of her pa
 ternal grandmother\, Zina\, a Russian woman who fled the chaos of the 1917
  Revolution and rebuilt her life in Iran. There\, in a boarding house that
  becomes a refuge for other displaced women\, Zina forms an unbreakable bo
 nd with fellow outsiders from Russia and Iran\, women who support one anot
 her through childbirth\, illness\, poverty\, political upheaval\, and a pa
 ndemic. Amid this turmoil\, Zina's path crosses with the ambitious Reza Kh
 an\, the future Shah of Iran\, whose presence in her life becomes both an 
 escape and a source of enduring hardship and sorrow.\nSpanning decades and
  alternating between Zina's years in Russia and her later life in Iran\, t
 his sweeping novel asks: what does it mean to build a home and a family fr
 om nothing\, in the wreckage of empire and revolution?\nDrawing on her own
  family history and her lifelong engagement with themes of exile\, resilie
 nce\, and the search for home\, first explored in her internationally best
 selling memoir Prisoner of Tehran\, Nemat brings the same unflinching hone
 sty and tenderness to her grandmother's story that made her own so unforge
 ttable.\nJoin Marina Nemat for an intimate conversation about inheritance\
 , chosen family\, and the quiet heroism of women who have had to build the
 ir lives twice.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for purch
 ase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nMarina Nemat\nFarah Heron\nRead more:\
 nMistress of the Persian Boarding House\nPrisoner of Tehran\nRemember Me T
 omorrow\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nConcourse Event Space\, North Y
 ork Central Library (5120 Yonge St)\, Lower Level\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00p
 m\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket po
 licy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the greatest number of peop
 le have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until
  capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\nAccessibility:\n
 TPL is committed to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability an
 d would like to request accommodation for this event\, please contact acce
 ssibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the ev
 ent.\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we 
 host local and international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversatio
 n about their new books and big ideas.\nThis event is also part of TPL's p
 rogramming series\,\nIslamic History and Culture\n.\nThis series aims to f
 oster a greater understanding and appreciation of Muslim communities' inva
 luable contributions to our shared history and identity. Join us in celebr
 ating the diversity that strengthens our community and makes our city a mo
 re vibrant and inclusive place for all.\n***\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a bri
 ef survey following the program. Questions about how the library handles y
 our information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space\, North York C
 entral Library (5120 Yonge St)\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b7952cbfe80d71a47342
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Robert Harris: Agrippa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T200000
UID:6a85b75e2cbfe80d71a4733f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents bestselling novelist Robert Harris in conversatio
 n with Ian Brown at the Toronto Reference Library's Appel Salon.\nWhat doe
 s it cost to build an empire\, and what does it cost the men who build it 
 for someone else? In his gripping new novel\nAgrippa\n\, Robert Harris ret
 urns to ancient Rome to chronicle the tale of Agrippa\, the commoner who w
 ill become the merciless agent of Emperor Augustus’s ambition. Now fifty
 \, ailing\, alone\, and betrayed by his wife's infidelity\, Agrippa retrea
 ts to his villa on the Bay of Naples to write his memoirs. But to stir up 
 the past is dangerous\, especially when that past includes the epic confli
 ct with Mark Antony and Cleopatra\, the great naval battle of Actium\, and
  decades spent as the loyal shadow to a man history remembers as a god.\nJ
 oin one of the world's most acclaimed historical novelists for an evening 
 of ambition\, empire\, and the perilous friendship at the heart of Rome's 
 transformation from republic to autocracy.\nQ&A and book signing to follow
 . Books available for purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nRobert Harr
 is\nIan Brown\nRead more:\nAgrippa\nConclave\nImperium\nSeventy : A Diary 
 of My Seventy-First Year\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nBram and Bluma
  Appel Salon\, Toronto Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 2nd floor\nT
 ime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registratio
 n required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the g
 reatest number of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed
  until 6:45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first ser
 ved.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available for purchase (debit/credit only).\nAccess
 ibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a dis
 ability and would like to request accommodation for this event\, please co
 ntact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior
  to the event.\n***\nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\,
  where we host local and international authors\, artists and thinkers in c
 onversation about their new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
