BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Working With Your Go To Emotional State
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T150000
UID:6a96f5deb885961432879469@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Most of us have a\n"go-to emotion."\nIt is the emotion that sh
 ows up automatically when we feel hurt or overwhelmed. That emotion can be
 \nanger\, anxiety\, depression\, guilt\, shame\, or even emotional numbnes
 s.\nIn this interactive presentation\, we will explore how your go-to emot
 ion developed\, what purpose it serves\, and offer techniques on how to re
 spond from a more measured space.\nJoin Ann Schnurr\, a Registered Psychot
 herapist with more than 25 years of experience\, as she supports adults to
  understand their go-to emotion for greater emotional resilience\, healthi
 er relationships\, and a deeper connection with self.\nRegistration is enc
 ouraged\nvia the library’s website.\nDrop-ins welcome until capacity is 
 reached.  For more information contact the Business Science & Technology d
 esk at 416-395-5613\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96f5deb885961432879469
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty Coffee: From Your First Brew to Barista
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T153000
UID:6a91c1d96383850d1b24760e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to take your love of coffee beyond a cup of cappuccino? T
 hinking about opening your own café or launching a coffee brand? Explore 
 real-world career paths in coffee - from café barista to roaster to coffe
 e entrepreneur. Find your entry point in this industry and learn about wha
 t works\, what doesn’t\, and what to avoid. This introductory workshop 
 will include a mini guided tasting experience.\nPresented by Hong Dai\, ow
 ner of Another Land Coffee\, a specialty coffee shop located in North York
 \, with over 15 years of experience in the specialty coffee and hospitalit
 y industry.\nThis program is part of TPL Small Business Month.
LOCATION:Oakwood Village Library and Arts Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91c1d96383850d1b24760e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Revitalizing Biodiversity in a Toronto Ravine on Public and Privat
 e Land – The Nordheimer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T190000
UID:6a557a85e9de6536001b836d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this presentation\, environmental researcher Susan Aaron wi
 ll explore the following questions: What is a ravine--historically and tod
 ay--as a base for natural revitalization and water retention and human and
  wildlife use? How do ravines reinvent what a city is\, as having a natura
 l base rather than a concrete one? And how might ravines inform us of the 
 linkages across public and private land\, informing both biodiversity and
  sustainability?
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a557a85e9de6536001b836d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
