BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Craft Club: Digital Creations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T163000
UID:69c5649b2866a5b4884491f9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Malvern Library's Craft Club runs twice a month on Tuesdays. 
 Basic supplies provided for learners.\nFirst session\n:\nJoin us in the Di
 gital Innovation Hub to make a crafting-related goodie to take home.\nOnli
 ne r\negistration required\nand opens one month in advance at 9am (12pm if
  this falls on a Sunday\, and the next business day if this falls on a ho
 liday).\nSecond session:\nDo you knit\, crochet\, hand-sew\, cross-stitch\
 , or embroider? Or are you looking to learn? Join us to stitch\, chat\, a
 nd have some fun while watching a cozy film.\nDrop-in.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c5649b2866a5b4884491f9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Investing Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T150000
UID:69e91f36fca21471b7f0027d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:PLEASE NOTE NEW FAIRVIEW LOCATION DUE TO HILLCREST JULY 27 CLO
 SING FOR REPAIRS.\nNew to investing? Learn the basics of this important pa
 rt of financial literacy\, including how to save with\nthe goal of investi
 ng\, types of investments\, how to open an account\, types of accounts\, h
 ow to avoid financial frauds and scams\, and more.\nPresented by the\nCana
 dian Investment Regulatory Organization\n(CIRO) a national self-regulatory
  organization that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers a
 nd trading activity on Canada's debt and equity marketplace.\nRegistration
  is encouraged\n. Drop-ins welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Program Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e91f36fca21471b7f0027d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T130000
UID:69e92c5bbd9a3c316a54b259@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Fridays\, join us for crafts 
 (11am - 1pm)\, exercise (11:30am - 12:30pm)\, and Ozzy the therapy dog (al
 ternate Fridays).\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participan
 ts. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is i
 n collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e92c5bbd9a3c316a54b259
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
