BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reschedule:  Artists in the Library:  Woodland Sunflower Felt Coll
 age
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T200000
UID:6a7e5d66b20478002992c363@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 1 of a series of workshops for adults\, exploring local f
 lora through embroidery and felt collage. Hosted by Artist in the Library\
 , Sarah Zanchetta.\nRegistration is required. Space is limited.\nPlease no
 te: Registered participant spaces will be held for 15 minutes after which 
 drop-ins will be allowed.\nPlease note: This is a rescheduled program for 
 Wed\, Sept 30\, 2026. The new date is Oct 1st\, 2026.\nMeet the Resident:\
 nSarah Zanchetta (she/they) is a queer textile artist and educator whose p
 ractice dives into the loss of connection and knowledge of poisonous plant
 s in North America. Zanchetta uses textiles\, texts\, and hosts community 
 workshops to create intimate works and spaces where we can unfold our curi
 osities\, care and anxieties about what grows beside our feet. She holds 
 a Master of Visual Studies from the University of Toronto (2023) and a BFA
  from OCAD University (2018).\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e5d66b20478002992c363
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cercle de conversation : Parlons cinéma ! French Conversation Cir
 cle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T193000
UID:6a833e0dbe1482002987eb5e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:[English version follows]\nPratiquez votre français en explor
 ant le monde du cinéma francophone.\nRegardez le film chez vous\n\, ensui
 te assistez à la rencontre pour discuter du film. Tous les niveaux sont b
 ienvenus. Les places sont limitées donc vous devez vous inscrire.\nPour l
 e mois de septembre\, nous allons discuter du film\nClose\n(Belgique\, 202
 2). Le film est disponible sur la plateforme\nKanopy\n. Le film est en fra
 nçais avec l'option de mettre les sous-titres en anglais.\nPractice your 
 French and explore the world of French-language cinema. Every month we mee
 t to discuss a French-language film that you\nwatch at home\nbefore the me
 eting. All levels are welcome. Please register as places are limited.\nFor
  the month of September\, we will discuss the film\nClose\n(Belgium\, 2022
 ). The film is available to stream for free with your TPL library card on\
 nKanopy\n. The film is presented in French with the option to add the Engl
 ish subtitles.\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal information 
 on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public 
 Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will 
 only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.
  Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed
  to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Stre
 et\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nACCESSIBILITÉ\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou aut
 omatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d’int
 ervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur demande
 . Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’avance à
  :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Meeting Room B1 (Lower Level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a833e0dbe1482002987eb5e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
