BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club de lecture français
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T200000
UID:6a904f7caafa6100295f84fa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Choisissez un livre français\, de votre genre préféré\, e
 t apportez-le à notre club de lecture pour en discuter !\nNous parlerons
  de ce que nous avons aime (ou moins aime) et nous vous dirons si nous le 
 recommandons à d'autres lecteurs francophones.\nVeuillez noter que ce p
 rogramme s’adresse aux personnes francophones ainsi qu’à celles ayant
  un niveau avancé en français. Il est nécessaire de pouvoir lire\, disc
 uter et critiquer un livre avec une aisance de communication en français.
 \nSi vous souhaitez pratiquer votre français mais que vous avez plutôt u
 n niveau débutant ou intermédiaire\, nous vous encourageons à découvri
 r nos\ncercles de conversation\n.\nAccessibilité:\nLe sous-titrage en dir
 ect ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les servic
 es d’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles s
 ur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l
 ’avance à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\nInformation Collection Notice
 :\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publi
 c Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20
 (d). The information will only be used for event and program registration\
 , delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your in
 formation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 41
 6-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904f7caafa6100295f84fa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Interventions in Our Landscape by Karen Sekika
 wa and Stephanie Calvet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260902T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T235959
UID:6a90690658433600542b8713@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of September\, Interventions in our Lands
 cape by artists Karen Sekikawa and Stephanie Calvet is on display at North
  York Central Library branch.\nKaren Sekikawa and Stephanie Calvet work at
  the intersection of architecture\, photography\, and design. Trained as a
 rchitects and based in Toronto\, they share a deep appreciation for cultur
 e and the built environment\, often exploring neighbourhoods both locally 
 and abroad. Their individual creative practices enrich their photography
 —Karen draws on her Japanese heritage through ikebana (flower arrangemen
 t)\, while Stephanie reconnects with design through urban sketching in pen
  and ink.\nKaren Sekikawa and Stephanie Calvet draw inspiration from archi
 tecture\, street life\, and built elements within the landscape. Their arc
 hitectural background is reflected in their photography\, which emphasizes
  form\, texture\, pattern\, light and shadow. Their approach leans toward 
 graphic compositions\, often highlighting abstracted details or framing ne
 w perspectives. They aim to provoke curiosity\, encouraging viewers to pau
 se\, reflect and appreciate the unique and see the familiar in a new light
 .\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Pub
 lic Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at loca
 tions across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural 
 interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed d
 uring North York Central Library open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd floor Gallery space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90690658433600542b8713
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
