UID:6a9082403b6c71003e5bcdbc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This unique​ information seminar informs people with start
 ups\, influencers\, artists\, entertainers and inventors about their inte
 llectual property rights. The presentation shares knowledge about the vari
 ous forms of IP assets– copyright\, trademark\, patents\, trade secrets\
 , contracts– with real world examples with multiple industries. IP plann
 ing and protection strategies will be explained in a fun and interesting p
 rogram by including magical effects during the presentation.\nThis progr
 am is part of Small Business Month.\nRegistration required.\nDrop-ins are 
 welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
