BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Speaking for Newcomers: Communicate with Confidence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T180000
UID:6a919d9860ccaf01c021a79c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Communicating clearly and confidently is a skill that everyone
  should have. For newcomers\, public speaking can feel especially daunting
  when navigating a new language or cultural expectations. This session is 
 designed to help you overcome those challenges and approach public speakin
 g with confidence. Along many educational and professional paths in Canada
 \, giving presentations is often a requirement. This session will provide 
 an overview of how to design and deliver presentations\, while also offeri
 ng practical tips and techniques for speaking clearly and effectively in a
  new environment. Presented by Victoria Tung.\nThis program is part of Sma
 ll Business Month and the Newcomer Entrepreneurship Initiative.
LOCATION:Annette Street\, Lower level\, auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a919d9860ccaf01c021a79c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Specialty Coffee: From Your First Brew to Barista
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T150000
UID:6a91c5b357c264087ad4810d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Want to take your love of coffee beyond a cup of cappuccino
 ? Thinking about opening your own café or launching a coffee brand? Explo
 re real-world career paths in coffee - from café barista to roaster to co
 ffee entrepreneur. Find your entry point in this industry and learn about 
 what works\, what doesn’t\, and what to avoid.\nPresented by Hong Dai\, 
 owner of Another Land Coffee\, a specialty coffee shop located in North Yo
 rk\, with over 15 years of experience in the specialty coffee and hospital
 ity industry.\nSpace is limited - registration is required.\nThis program 
 is part of TPL Small Business Month.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91c5b357c264087ad4810d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
