BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Friends of the Arthur Conan Doyle Collection: 2026 Cameron Hol
 lyer Memorial Lecture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T160000
UID:6a91cd3f57c264087ad483e1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Sultan and the Detective: Sherlock Holmes’ Curious Adven
 tures in the Ottoman Empire\nHistorical fact: the last great Ottoman sulta
 n\, Abdülhamid II\, fell asleep each night to the adventures of Sherlock 
 Holmes\, read aloud to him by a palace attendant. This unlikely obsession 
 is the starting point for Andrew Finkel's novel\nThe Adventure of the Seco
 nd Wife.\nIn this talk\, Finkel explores how the world of Arthur Conan Doy
 le intersected with the late Ottoman Empire\, and what this reveals about 
 storytelling\, translation\, and the unexpected ways stories travel across
  languages\, cultures\, and empires to take on meanings the author never i
 ntended.\nAndrew Finkel is a journalist and author who has reported from T
 urkey for major international outlets including\nThe Times\, The Economist
 \, TIME\, CNN\,\nand\nThe New York Times\n. He co-founded Platform24 (P24)
 \, an Istanbul-based NGO that supports independent journalism and freedom 
 of expression\, and is the author of\nTurkey: What Everyone Needs to Know\
 n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, Ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91cd3f57c264087ad483e1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cyanotype Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T143000
UID:6a89a624feae9600380742ec@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What materials and processes existed before Adobe Photoshop? J
 oin us for a hands-on analog image making workshop to create a Cyanotype. 
 The Cyanotype is a photographic printing technique sensitive to a limited 
 near ultraviolet and blue light spectrum. It involves layering objects and
  transparencies. All are welcome!\nWe will supply all materials\, but feel
  free to bring an object or 2D silhouette for a contact print.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room (First Floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a89a624feae9600380742ec
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to OnShape (Adults)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T190000
UID:6a94652629a7dd0d6747c945@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in creating your own 3D models? Join us for an intr
 oduction to Onshape\, a powerful cloud-based Computer-Aided Design (CAD) s
 oftware used by engineers\, designers\, and makers around the world.\nIn t
 his beginner-friendly workshop\, participants will learn the fundamentals 
 of 3D modeling\, including how to navigate the Onshape interface\, create 
 basic sketches\, and turn those sketches into 3D objects using extrude and
  extrude cut features. No previous CAD experience is required.\nBy the end
  of the program\, participants will have created their own simple 3D model
  and gained the skills needed to continue exploring CAD design on their ow
 n.\nBasic Computer skills are Mandatory\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a94652629a7dd0d6747c945
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Use Gamification to Achieve Business Objectives - for found
 ers and newcomers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T200000
UID:6a91dabb4cb69d003e241a90@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by eduTechnoz\, this interactive workshop equips startu
 p and newcomer founders to harness gamification for business goals by infl
 uencing human behavior. Participants will learn core principles\, the 'Cir
 cle' framework\, and strategies to overcome challenges using game mechanic
 s. A relevant case study and collaborative discussion help craft tailored 
 solutions\, followed by a Q&A session for deeper insights.\nAll are welcom
 e!\nThis program is part of Small Business Month and the Newcomer Entrepre
 neurship Initiative.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91dabb4cb69d003e241a90
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
